{
 "cells": [
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# Resume–Job Matching: Dataset Exploration\n","\n","A small, runnable exploration of the proposal dataset. It checks schemas, joins recorded pairs, summarizes the overall compatibility score as a proxy label, and demonstrates a single B0 TF–IDF comparison. It does not use dataset component subscores as model features.\n","\n","Download `cv.csv`, `job.csv`, and `matches.csv` as described in [`data/README.md`](../data/README.md). Run from the repository root or `notebooks/`. The notebook does not display resume text. Results are exploratory, not hiring performance."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["from pathlib import Path\n","import json\n","import numpy as np\n","import pandas as pd\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","\n","cwd = Path.cwd()\n","ROOT = cwd if (cwd / 'data').is_dir() else cwd.parent\n","DATA = ROOT / 'data'\n","paths = {name: DATA / f'{name}.csv' for name in ('cv', 'job', 'matches')}\n","missing = [str(path) for path in paths.values() if not path.is_file()]\n","if missing:\n","    raise FileNotFoundError('Dataset files missing: ' + ', '.join(missing) + '. See data/README.md.')\n","cv_df, job_df, matches_df = (pd.read_csv(paths[name], low_memory=False) for name in ('cv', 'job', 'matches'))\n","print('Loaded row counts:', {'cv': len(cv_df), 'job': len(job_df), 'matches': len(matches_df)})"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 1. Schema check\n","\n","Only headers and counts are shown; do not print whole resume or job text columns."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["for name, frame in [('CV', cv_df), ('jobs', job_df), ('matches', matches_df)]:\n","    print(f'{name}: {frame.shape[0]:,} rows, {frame.shape[1]} columns')\n","    print('  ' + ', '.join(map(str, frame.columns)))\n","\ndef find_col(frame, aliases, required=True):\n","    lookup = {str(c).strip().lower(): c for c in frame.columns}\n","    for alias in aliases:\n","        if alias in lookup:\n","            return lookup[alias]\n","    if required:\n","        raise KeyError(f'Could not find one of {aliases}; available columns: {list(frame.columns)}')\n","    return None\n","\n","cv_id = find_col(cv_df, ['candidate_id', 'cv_id', 'resume_id', 'profile_id'])\n","cv_text = find_col(cv_df, ['resume_text', 'cv_text', 'resume', 'cv', 'profile_text'])\n","job_id = find_col(job_df, ['job_id', 'jobid', 'id'])\n","job_text = find_col(job_df, ['job_text', 'job_description', 'description', 'text'])\n","job_title = find_col(job_df, ['job_title', 'title', 'position'], required=False)\n","pair_cv_id = find_col(matches_df, ['candidate_id', 'cv_id', 'resume_id', 'profile_id'])\n","pair_job_id = find_col(matches_df, ['job_id', 'jobid'])\n","label_col = find_col(matches_df, ['final_score', 'compatibility_score', 'match_score', 'score'])\n","print('Required IDs, text fields, and overall proxy-score field resolved.')"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 2. Join recorded pairs and inspect the compatibility proxy\n","\n","The overall compatibility score is a graded proxy relevance label, not a human hiring judgment. Unrecorded pairs are unknown, not negative examples. Component subscores are intentionally excluded."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["cv_min = pd.DataFrame({'candidate_id': cv_df[cv_id].astype(str), 'resume_text': cv_df[cv_text].fillna('').astype(str)})\n","job_min = pd.DataFrame({'job_id': job_df[job_id].astype(str), 'job_text': job_df[job_text].fillna('').astype(str)})\n","if job_title:\n","    job_min['job_title'] = job_df[job_title].fillna('').astype(str)\n","else:\n","    job_min['job_title'] = ''\n","pairs = pd.DataFrame({'candidate_id': matches_df[pair_cv_id].astype(str), 'job_id': matches_df[pair_job_id].astype(str), 'proxy_score': pd.to_numeric(matches_df[label_col], errors='coerce')}).dropna(subset=['proxy_score'])\n","joined = pairs.merge(cv_min, on='candidate_id', how='inner').merge(job_min, on='job_id', how='inner')\n","print(f'Joinable recorded pairs: {len(joined):,}; candidates: {joined.candidate_id.nunique():,}; jobs: {joined.job_id.nunique():,}')\n","display(pd.DataFrame({'table':['CV','jobs','match records','joinable recorded pairs'], 'rows':[len(cv_df),len(job_df),len(matches_df),len(joined)]}))\n","display(joined['proxy_score'].describe().to_frame('compatibility proxy label'))\n","ax = joined['proxy_score'].plot(kind='hist', bins=40, figsize=(8,4), title='Recorded compatibility proxy-score distribution')\n","ax.set_xlabel('Dataset compatibility score'); ax.set_ylabel('Recorded-pair count'); plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 3. Optional structured-skill gap summary\n","\n","A skill not detected in structured resume skills is only *not evidenced in that field*; it does not mean the person lacks that ability. The overall compatibility score is not used as a model input here."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["def parse_skills(value):\n","    if value is None or (isinstance(value, float) and np.isnan(value)):\n","        return set()\n","    if isinstance(value, (list, tuple, set)):\n","        values = value\n","    else:\n","        raw = str(value).strip()\n","        if not raw:\n","            return set()\n","        try:\n","            values = json.loads(raw)\n","        except (json.JSONDecodeError, TypeError):\n","            values = [part.strip().strip('\\\"\\\'') for part in raw.strip('[]').split(',')]\n","        if isinstance(values, str):\n","            values = [values]\n","    if not isinstance(values, (list, tuple, set)):\n","        return set()\n","    return {' '.join(str(item).casefold().split()) for item in values if str(item).strip()}\n","\n","cv_skill_col = find_col(cv_df, ['clean_skills_json', 'clean_skills', 'candidate_skills', 'skills'], required=False)\n","job_skill_col = find_col(job_df, ['clean_skills_json', 'clean_skills', 'required_skills', 'skills'], required=False)\n","if cv_skill_col and job_skill_col:\n","    cv_skill_map = dict(zip(cv_df[cv_id].astype(str), cv_df[cv_skill_col].map(parse_skills)))\n","    job_skill_map = dict(zip(job_df[job_id].astype(str), job_df[job_skill_col].map(parse_skills)))\n","    skill_rows = joined[['candidate_id', 'job_id', 'proxy_score']].copy()\n","    skill_rows['resume_skills'] = skill_rows['candidate_id'].map(cv_skill_map)\n","    skill_rows['job_skills'] = skill_rows['job_id'].map(job_skill_map)\n","    skill_rows['shared_count'] = skill_rows.apply(lambda row: len(row.resume_skills & row.job_skills), axis=1)\n","    skill_rows['not_evidenced_count'] = skill_rows.apply(lambda row: len(row.job_skills - row.resume_skills), axis=1)\n","    display(skill_rows[['shared_count','not_evidenced_count']].describe())\n","else:\n","    print('Structured skill columns not found in both data tables; skipped.')"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 4. One-pair TF–IDF illustration (B0)\n","\n","This is a simple demonstration on one recorded pair, not a ranking benchmark. The grouped evaluation script is the appropriate place to compare B0/B1/B2. The dataset compatibility score is not used to fit TF–IDF."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["from sklearn.feature_extraction.text import TfidfVectorizer\n","from sklearn.metrics.pairwise import cosine_similarity\n","\n","sample = joined[(joined.resume_text.str.strip() != '') & (joined.job_text.str.strip() != '')].head(1)\n","if sample.empty:\n","    print('No non-empty joined resume/job text available for the demonstration.')\n","else:\n","    row = sample.iloc[0]\n","    posting = (str(row.job_title) + '\\n' + row.job_text).strip()\n","    matrix = TfidfVectorizer(ngram_range=(1, 2), stop_words='english').fit_transform([row.resume_text, posting])\n","    print(f'B0 TF–IDF cosine for one recorded pair: {cosine_similarity(matrix[0:1], matrix[1:2])[0, 0]:.4f}')\n","    print('Resume and job text are not displayed; this is not a benchmark metric.')"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Interpretation and next steps\n","\n","- The dataset score is a constructed proxy label, not ground-truth hiring outcome.\n","- Only recorded pairs are available; unrecorded pairs are unknown, not negatives.\n","- Do not use precomputed semantic/skill/title/category/experience/education subscores as model inputs.\n","- Use `experiments/grouped_matching_baselines/run.py` for source-group-disjoint B0/B1/B2 ranking. Heuristic source groups are not verified identity and exclusions may be biased.\n","- Avoid committing executed notebook outputs containing personal or sensitive text."]}
